  <h2>Decide What the Roof Needs to Do</h2>
  <p>Louvres rotate to adjust light and airflow; they do not necessarily retract to reveal open sky. Check how far the blades move and what stays overhead.</p>
  <p>Observe where the sun falls when you actually use the patio, particularly late in the day. Consider winter light into adjacent rooms. The Australian Government's <a href="https://www.yourhome.gov.au/passive-design/shading" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Your Home shading guidance</a> explains the role of orientation, season and climate.</p>
  <p>If your layout may change, compare a permanent roof with umbrellas and fabric awnings in our <a href="/guides/outdoor-shade-setup-for-patios-and-backyards-what-to-check-before-buying/">outdoor shade guide</a>.</p>

